## Session Recap — 2026-07-26 (cont'd) — v4.4.0 shipped, branch-guard `2>&1` bug found+fixed, #263 spec+grill

Continuation of the same day's #268/#266 work (below). Three more threads closed/opened:

**v4.4.0 released** via `/craft:release`: PR #314 (dev→main, MINOR — the one `feat:` commit
since v4.3.1 was #313's D7), full pipeline verified (CI, docs deploy, Homebrew tap, aggregator
sync all confirmed green). See the `milestone:` field above for full detail.

**`/finish` surfaced and fixed a real global-infra bug**: `~/.claude/hooks/branch-guard.sh`'s
coarse redirect-detection gate matched `2>&1`/`1>&2` (benign fd-duplication, used on nearly
every Bash call) as "a real redirect present," then re-scanned the whole original command and
misattributed an unrelated `->` arrow *inside an already-quoted commit message* as a
file-creation target — blocking legitimate commits like `git commit -m "...(7 -> 9)" 2>&1`.
Root-caused via direct synthetic hook invocation (`subprocess.run(["/bin/bash",
"branch-guard.sh"], input=payload)`, bypassing the Claude Code harness entirely) rather than
guessing from the rendered error text. One-line fix: exclude `&` from the coarse gate's
character class. Verified against 4 originally-failing cases (now pass) and 5 regression cases
(genuine `.py`/`.sh` file-creation redirects, `tee`, `/dev/null` — all still behave correctly).
This file lives outside any git repo (global `~/.claude/`), so nothing to commit here — the fix
is live immediately.

**#263 (RTK hook-ordering safety) spec'd + grilled**: found RTK is already installed globally
(contradicting the issue's own "don't install until verified" precondition) and that a
2026-07-07 internal proposal (`~/.claude/PROPOSAL-rtk-guard-safety.md`) had already partially
resolved the core question — but its citation of official Claude Code hook docs overstated what
those docs actually say (parallel execution: confirmed; no cross-hook input propagation: NOT
explicitly stated, corrected live during this grill by re-fetching the docs directly). Locked 4
decisions: add one lightweight live confirmatory test (now the primary evidence, not a
formality) · archive the original 5-task probe spec as superseded · add one narrow branch-guard
regression test for today's confirmed `2>&1` bug class · explicitly defer a wider speculative
audit of the guard's other patterns. Artifacts:
`docs/specs/SPEC-rtk-hook-safety-close-out-2026-07-26.md`,
`docs/specs/GRILL-rtk-hook-safety-close-out-2026-07-26.md` — **not yet implemented**, both new
untracked files pending the next session.

**Next:** implement the #263 close-out (live test → archive old spec → regression test →
TUTORIAL §4.2 rewrite → close #263), ideally with one more adversarial-review pass first per
the pattern that worked well for #268/#266 earlier today.

## Session Recap — 2026-07-26 — #268/#266 prompt-refiner: grilled, adversarially reviewed, re-scoped, shipped (PR #313)

Picked up the #268/#266 thread flagged as next action in the prior recap. Wrote a spec +
6-decision GRILL ledger covering #268's 3 remaining audit items (named Copy-for-elsewhere
destinations, `--scope global`, D7 smart-help cleanup) plus #266's multi-round grill-mode
design — then, before implementing, ran an adversarial review (code-review lens + design
lens, both `opus`) against the locked design. Both independently found it unbuildable/
unjustified:

- **Destinations item** — the proposed `{text, destination_intent}` return has no consumer;
  every caller (`do.md`, `brainstorm.md`, `plan/feature.md`, `arch/plan.md`, `orch.md`) is
  explicitly instructed to STOP on that branch, and standalone `/refine` has no caller at
  all. Also re-adds a category `refine.md` deliberately removed (clipboard/background-exec
  as "command-routing, not prompt-refining").
- **`--scope global`** — sound mechanism, but n=1 demand from one 2026-07-05 conversation
  turn, against 7 caller files of flag plumbing. Deferred pending a second independent ask.
- **#266 grill mode** — verified directly: `savant/src/plugin-api/skills/edit-loop/SKILL.md`
  shipped 2026-07-13 (savant #192), 8 days after #266's originating observation and 11 days
  before a 2026-07-24 audit comment that missed it and called #266 "still valid." craft's
  evidence for a *general-purpose* (non-manuscript) grill mode is n=0. Also: the proposed
  design's "apply immediately" contradicted `prompt-refiner/SKILL.md`'s own "NEVER write
  files" constraint, and delegating to `craft:grill`'s loop would have created an unguarded
  recursion (`grill` calls `prompt-refiner` by default on any quoted topic; the trigger
  phrase survives that round-trip). Closed #266 pointing at savant `edit-loop`.

Re-scoped to ship only D7 (smart-help `--refine` declaration + an exhaustive, file-path-keyed
Default Policy table fixing 3 stale display names and 2 missing live callers). Built in
`feature/prompt-refiner-smart-help-d7`, full suite green (2618 passed/0 failed), merged via
PR #313 (squash, dev). Post-merge doc check: `docs-staleness-check.sh` GREEN on all 4 phases;
`docs_detector.py` run on request, confirmed noisy-as-documented (~2700 false-positive hits,
none touching this change) — nothing to update.

Artifacts: `docs/specs/SPEC-prompt-refiner-remaining-2026-07-26.md`,
`docs/specs/GRILL-prompt-refiner-remaining-2026-07-26.md` (see its AMENDMENT section for the
full reversal record — decisions are marked withdrawn/deferred, not silently rewritten).

**Next:** no decided next action — #268/#266 thread is fully closed. Remaining backlog:
#263/#228/#213/#199/#108.

