## Session Recap — 2026-07-24/25 — #281 dev-edit deadlock fix (PR #305), #286 reference-scope guard (PR #306)

**Merged to dev, NOT yet released.** Continuation of the same session that shipped PR #303/#304;
two more issue fixes, both closed.

**#281 — `CRAFT_GUARD_ALLOW_DEV_EDIT` escape hatch** (PR #305, `b3befc7ac`): closed a self-referential
deadlock — creating/editing the `.claude/allow-once`/`allow-dev-edit` bypass marker that lets a user
pre-authorize a branch-guard bypass was itself gated by the same guard it was meant to bypass.
Adversarially reviewed the issue's own proposed fix (verify `permissionDecision: "ask"` in headless
mode) and judged it unverifiable from this environment; reused the proven `CRAFT_GUARD_ALLOW_FORCE_DELETE`
pattern from #168 instead — an env-var pre-authorization escape hatch, structurally safe because
Bash-tool env exports don't propagate into the hook's separate subprocess. Added to all 3
`_confirm "*_guard_bypass"` call sites in `branch-guard.sh` + 7 new tests (134→141/141 total) +
`skills/dev/git/SKILL.md` doc update. Hit the guard's own recursive meta-friction along the way:
editing `branch-guard.sh` was blocked by auto-mode's classifier (a stale `settings.local.json`
Edit-permission rule scoped to a now-deleted #168 worktree path); the user resolved it directly by
adding a glob-scoped permission rule after a brainstorm-formatted proposal (declined to self-modify
`settings.local.json`).

**#286 — `reference-scope-guard.sh`** (PR #306, `7c94e77d3`): new advisory-only (never-blocking)
PreToolUse hook warning when a Write/Edit targets `~/.claude/reference/` with a filename that
doesn't match its naming convention (lowercase kebab-case, no `.html`, no `SPEC-*`/`GRILL-*`/
`BRAINSTORM-*` prefix — those belong in `docs/specs/`). Verified the problem empirically before
building: real pre-existing violations already exist in `~/.claude/reference/`
(`SPEC-proof-tutorial-tooling.md`, `tutor-cookbook.html`, etc.), confirming the issue's premise.
Wired into `install-guards.sh`'s existing 3-part pattern (install_hook, `Edit|Write`-only
`PreToolUse` registration, `guards.json` seed) alongside `branch-guard`/`no-switch-guard`. New
13-case e2e suite `tests/test_reference_scope_guard.sh`. One bug found and fixed pre-commit:
`basename` misinterpreted a leading-dash filename as a CLI flag — fixed with `basename -- "..."`.

**Verification:** full suite 2615 passed/0 failed (both PRs); `test_branch_guard.sh` 141/141;
`test_no_switch_guard.sh` 39/39 (both unaffected by #286's change); `test_reference_scope_guard.sh`
13/13 (repo copy and installed hook). Both worktrees removed, local branches deleted, remote
branches auto-deleted via `--delete-branch`. Issues #281 and #286 closed (dev-merge doesn't
auto-close — both closed manually with a PR reference).

