Prior: Dependabot batch resolved + dev/main sync 2026-07-02 — reviewed [#255](https://github.com/Data-Wise/craft/pull/255) (zod 3→4) and [#256](https://github.com/Data-Wise/craft/pull/256) (typescript 5→6) via `/review` (medium effort, precision): zero correctness findings, but discovered craft-mcp's `zod` prod dep has ZERO direct imports in `mcp/src/` (all references live in `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`'s own bundled copy or SDK node_modules). Merged #256 clean, #255 after a rebase (shared `mcp/package-lock.json`). **Root-cause discovered mid-review:** `.github/dependabot.yml` had no `target-branch`, so it defaulted to craft's GitHub default branch (`main`) — #255/#256 merged straight into `main`, bypassing the `main←dev←feature` model and drifting `dev` behind by 5 commits. Fixed via user-directed 3-step plan: (1) synced `dev←main` to absorb the bumps (merge commit, 2 files); (2) opened [#257](https://github.com/Data-Wise/craft/pull/257) on `feature/drop-zod-dep` (worktree, since removed) — dropped the unused direct `zod` dep (stays installed transitively via SDK's own `zod: ^3.25 || ^4.0` range) + added `target-branch: "dev"` to both Dependabot ecosystems; verified via `npm install` (0 vulnerabilities, zod still resolvable) + `npm run smoke` (20/20 PASS, bundle size unchanged 536.3kb) before pushing — merged to `dev`; (3) cleared the 3 remaining orphaned Dependabot PRs still targeting `main` (opened before the config fix): [#254](https://github.com/Data-Wise/craft/pull/254) (@types/node 22→26, clean), [#252](https://github.com/Data-Wise/craft/pull/252) (markdownlint-cli2 0.14→0.23, after `gh pr update-branch`), [#253](https://github.com/Data-Wise/craft/pull/253) (esbuild 0.25→0.28, after `@dependabot rebase` to resolve a `mcp/package.json` conflict with merged #254) — all merged to `main` on green CI (only required check is "Validate Plugin Structure"; the failing `dependabot` auto-merge-helper check is non-required and was correctly not treated as a blocker). Fin