**A0 FINDING 2026-07-04 (read-only investigation, no code/spec changes):** Checked whether superpowers `brainstorming` actually hard-gate-preempts craft (C2, was "Critical · unverified"). **Confirmed real but softer than Critical, and narrower in scope.** Mechanism: superpowers ships its own `SessionStart` hook (`hooks/session-start`, matcher `startup|clear|compact`) that unconditionally injects the full `using-superpowers` skill body as `<EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>` context on every top-level session start/clear/compact — regardless of task type (confirmed live: fired this session on a read-only doc-review request). That body contains a hard mandate ("IF A SKILL APPLIES...YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE") and an explicit priority rule ("'Let's build X' → superpowers:brainstorming first, then implementation skills") with zero awareness of craft's own `skills/workflow/brainstorm/SKILL.md`, which targets nearly the same trigger words ("brainstorm", "design a feature", "draft a spec") — a genuine unresolved entry-point collision, same class as C1. **Two mitigants found via a live subagent test:** (1) enforcement is prompt-level only — inspected `settings.json` `PreToolUse` hooks directly (`branch-guard`, `version-sync-hook`, `no-switch-guard`, `rtk`); none gate Write/Edit on prior skill invocation, so nothing technically blocks implementation before brainstorming runs, unlike craft's own hook-enforced guards. (2) it does not propagate to subagents — a fresh dispatched agent's context contained only the bare name `superpowers:using-superpowers`, not its injected body, meaning craft's own `orchestrate-dispatch`/`plan-orchestrator` background-agent architecture is untouched by this mechanism; only the interactive top-level session gets primed. **Recommendation for whenever the bigger effort gets scoped:** downgrade C2 severity from Critical to Medium (scoped to top-level interactive turns only); A4/A6 don't drop out entirely as the proposal's pre-pause note speculated, but their scope shrinks to documentation of precedence — no hook rewrite needed.

