✅ Closed 2026-07-06 (no build): **Orchestration token-usage hooks backlog (captured 2026-07-02) — grilled and rejected.** Source: [`docs/internal/TUTORIAL-orchestration-and-skill-eval-loop.md`](docs/internal/TUTORIAL-orchestration-and-skill-eval-loop.md) §11 proposed 3 hooks (live token field in run markers, `--report` flag on `/craft:orch`, `cost_weighted` delta in `status`). Two review passes (backend/architecture + interface/CLI-contract, mirroring this session's own adversarial-review lenses) found: hook 1 infeasible (no live token-introspection API exists — the orchestrator is a prompt-driven LLM session, not a process with self-usage access); hook 3 structurally uncomputable for an in-progress run (report script needs `end_ts` + flushed `agent-*.jsonl`, neither exists mid-run); hooks 1+2 collapse to a single feasible post-hoc `--token-report` flag. **Closed anyway** — the surviving flag doesn't fix the problem that motivated the backlog (retroactive analysis of 9 old parity-gate markers failed because zero `agent-*.jsonl` transcripts survived; a new flag only helps future runs, not that gap), and it duplicates the accounting-tooling category this session already removed (`scripts/quota-persist.sh` et al., "I don't use quota anymore"). Full reasoning: [`GRILL-orchestrate-token-usage-hooks-2026-07-06.md`](docs/specs/GRILL-orchestrate-token-usage-hooks-2026-07-06.md). No code changes.

